1. Fashionpedia ontology (category and attribute vocabulary, supercategories, taxonomy ids)
   ontologies/fashion/fashion.ttl is derived from the Fashionpedia ontology.
   Fashionpedia: https://fashionpedia.github.io/home/index.html
   Terms of use: https://fashionpedia.github.io/home/data_license.html
   "The annotations in the Fashionpedia dataset along with the ontology, and the websites belong to
   the Fashionpedia and are licensed under a Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 License."
   License: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
   ontologies/fashion/fashion.ttl is licensed under CC BY 4.0. The MIT-0 license of this repository
   does not apply to that file; it says so in its first lines and in dcterms:rights. The
   Fashionpedia authors do not endorse this sample.
   Attribution: Fashionpedia ontology by Menglin Jia, Mengyun Shi, Mikhail Sirotenko, Yin Cui,
   Claire Cardie, Bharath Hariharan, Hartwig Adam, Serge Belongie. "Fashionpedia: Ontology,
   Segmentation, and an Attribute Localization Dataset". ECCV 2020.
   Changes made for this repository (CC BY 4.0 requires that modifications are indicated): the flat
   category/attribute catalog is expressed as an OWL 2 ontology (groups and categories as classes,
   attribute families as classes with attribute values as named individuals, one has<Family> object
   property per family); Fashionpedia's family and supercategory names are rendered as class and
   property names (for example "textile finishing, manufacturing techniques" becomes TextileFinishing
   and hasTextileFinishing, "animal" becomes AnimalMaterial); parenthesized qualifiers of value names
   are kept as skos:prefLabel and dropped from rdfs:label; an applicability matrix is added as
   property domains; hasPart links garments to parts/closures/decorations; four jewelry categories
   that Fashionpedia does not have (earring, necklace, bracelet, ring) are added to its "others"
   group, each marked with a skos:editorialNote; a brand knowledge-graph schema (Look, Item,
   Statement, Article, Line, Brand and their relations) is added, with the fo:visual and
   fo:conceptId annotations; a closed vocabulary of occasions (the class Occasion, nine named
   individuals with labels, definitions and skos:hiddenLabel matching words, and the property for
   from Look to Occasion) is added, each term marked with a skos:editorialNote. See
   ontologies/fashion/README.md.
   Definitions: the Fashionpedia catalog has names, supercategories, levels and taxonomy ids, but
   no description text. Every definition in fashion.ttl (rdfs:comment, skos:definition) was
   written for this sample by its authors.
   The catalog file the ontology is built from is data/demo/category_attributes_descriptions.json
   in the Fashionpedia API repository, https://github.com/KMnP/fashionpedia-api. The build script
   (ontologies/fashion/build_fashion_ontology.py) downloads it; it is not included here.
